            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}.rn{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,"SF Pro Text",sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:4px 2px}.rn h1{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}.rn h2{font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}.rn ul{margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px}.rn li{margin-bottom:7px}.rn code{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.rn{color:#e8e8ed}}</style><div class="rn"><h1>Rein 0.8.8</h1>
<ul>
<li><b>Tidy your menu bar.</b> New in Settings → General: "Hide extra menu bar icons" adds a slim ⋮ divider and a ‹ chevron to the menu bar. ⌘-drag any icons you want hidden to the left of the divider — the chevron tucks them away and brings them back on a click. Revealed icons re-hide automatically after 15 seconds (optional). Turning the feature off — or quitting Rein — instantly restores every icon.</li>
</ul></div>
]]></description>
