        </item>
        <item>
            <title>0.8.6</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 14:21:23 +1200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>17</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}.rn{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,"SF Pro Text",sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:4px 2px}.rn h1{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}.rn h2{font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}.rn ul{margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px}.rn li{margin-bottom:7px}.rn code{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.rn{color:#e8e8ed}}</style><div class="rn"><h1>Rein 0.8.6</h1>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed a wrong automatic quality drop.</b> Starting a new cast could misread the previous session's state as a playback failure, silently blacklist the TV from full quality, and land at 720p. The stale signal is now cleared when a cast starts, and any wrongly-remembered blacklist heals on your next cast.</li>
</ul></div>
]]></description>
